  "html": "<section class=\"lesson-page\"> <div class=\"course-intro-card\"> <span class=\"exam-badge\"> TASK-BASED SIMULATION </span> <h2> Statement of Cash Flows </h2> <p> Classify cash transactions and calculate net cash provided by operating activities. </p> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-card\"> <h3> Company Information </h3> <div class=\"tbs-data-row\"> <span> Net Income </span> <strong> $120,000 </strong> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-row\"> <span> Depreciation Expense </span> <strong> $25,000 </strong> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-row\"> <span> Increase in Accounts Receivable </span> <strong> $18,000 </strong> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-row\"> <span> Decrease in Inventory </span> <strong> $10,000 </strong> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-row\"> <span> Increase in Accounts Payable </span> <strong> $7,000 </strong> </div> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-card\"> <h3> Part 1 · Classify the Transactions </h3> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs2-q1\"> 1. Cash paid to purchase equipment </label> <select id=\"tbs2-q1\" class=\"tbs-input\"> <option value=\"\"> Select classification </option> <option value=\"Operating\"> Operating </option> <option value=\"Investing\"> Investing </option> <option value=\"Financing\"> Financing </option> </select> </div> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs2-q2\"> 2. Cash received from issuing common stock </label> <select id=\"tbs2-q2\" class=\"tbs-input\"> <option value=\"\"> Select classification </option> <option value=\"Operating\"> Operating </option> <option value=\"Investing\"> Investing </option> <option value=\"Financing\"> Financing </option> </select> </div> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs2-q3\"> 3. Cash collected from customers </label> <select id=\"tbs2-q3\" class=\"tbs-input\"> <option value=\"\"> Select classification </option> <option value=\"Operating\"> Operating </option> <option value=\"Investing\"> Investing </option> <option value=\"Financing\"> Financing </option> </select> </div> </div> <div class=\"tbs-data-card\"> <h3> Part 2 · Operating Cash Flow </h3> <p> Using the indirect method and the information above, calculate net cash provided by operating activities. </p> <div class=\"tbs-question\"> <label for=\"tbs2-q4\"> 4. Net Cash Provided by Operating Activities </label> <input type=\"number\" id=\"tbs2-q4\" class=\"tbs-input\" placeholder=\"Enter amount\"> </div> </div> <div id=\"tbs2-result\"></div> </section>",
  "explanation": "<div class=\"tbs-results\"> <div class=\"key-points\"> <h3> Correct Answers </h3> <p> 1. Equipment purchase: <strong>Investing</strong> </p> <p> 2. Issue common stock: <strong>Financing</strong> </p> <p> 3. Customer collections: <strong>Operating</strong> </p> <p> 4. Net operating cash flow: <strong>$144,000</strong> </p> </div> <div class=\"example-box\"> <h3> Operating Cash Flow Calculation </h3> <p> Net Income = $120,000 </p> <p> + Depreciation = $25,000 </p> <p> − Increase in Accounts Receivable = $18,000 </p> <p> + Decrease in Inventory = $10,000 </p> <p> + Increase in Accounts Payable = $7,000 </p> <div class=\"formula-box\"> $120,000 + $25,000 − $18,000 + $10,000 + $7,000 = $144,000 </div> </div> </div>",
